cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or software, please cite it as below."
title: "Anatolian Crossroads: A Memory Graph from Neolithic Symbols to Iron Age Inscriptions (macro dataset and visualization)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Karaca
    given-names: "Doğan"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-02
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/dgnkaraca-hub/anatolian-crossroads"
abstract: >-
  A comparative digital-humanities network spanning 10 Anatolian and Upper
  Mesopotamian sites (9600-700 BCE). Sites connect only through geographic
  corridors, explicit comparative pairs and shared concept nodes; interpretive
  claims live in a separate interpretation layer with a four-tier confidence
  model. Every node and edge is sourced. Data files (JSON/CSV) are released
  under CC BY 4.0; application code under MIT.
keywords:
  - digital humanities
  - network analysis
  - Anatolia
  - Upper Mesopotamia
  - Neolithic
  - Iron Age
  - epigraphy
  - uncertainty modelling
  - "Göbekli Tepe"
  - "Sam'al"
